I'm even madder because I can see it!

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:35.410
I'm going to catch you, no matter what!

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:36.580
Tsurugi.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:37.580
Yes?

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.160
When ya lift up yer pole

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.500
and ya feel it get heavy, stop for a sec.

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:47.580
The shrimp will realize somethin's wrong
and jump back right onto the hook.

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.910
Ya keep pullin' too much.

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:53.200
It's hard for ya to get the timin' down, right?

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:56.250
Wow, President...

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:58.250
I'll give it a try!

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:06.700
I-Is it about time?

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:12.040
Take advantage of the pole bendin', too.
Stop it right when it starts bendin'.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:13.160
Okay.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:15.370
Yup. Just like that.

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:26.450
Ya got one.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:27.700
Here it comes!

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:30.700
Lift it up slowly. It can fall off pretty easy.

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:32.450
Right!

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:40.870
I did it!

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:43.370
Congratulations.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:47.540
Ha! Take that! I told you I'd catch you!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:50.870
Now I'm gonna catch the
rest of you! Just you wait!

00:16:55.790 --> 00:17:00.660
What're ya doin'? I told ya
the hook comes off easily.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.120
Gently... Gently...

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:16.120
See? It's thrillin' and excitin', right?

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:22.200
Yes, actually. It looked a lot easier,
but I guess it's pretty hard.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:25.000
Once ya get the hang of it, it's pretty easy.

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:27.080
Ya caught the next one pretty easy, didn't ya?

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:29.370
Oh, yeah...

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:32.080
I thought they were dumb little shrimps,

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:36.750
but maybe how fun fishing is has nothing
to do with the size of what you catch.

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:39.410
So how do I get this off?

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:41.250
Ya rip it off with yer bare hands.

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:43.370
I can't touch that with my bare hands!

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:46.290
Okay, fine. Here're some gloves.

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:49.000
Use some tweezers to gently get it off.

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:03.250
Wow, it's big!

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:08.830
Hey, this one's arms are short.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:12.330
That one's a female.
It's got some eggs in its belly.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:14.950
Whoa! There are a lot of bubbles!

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:18.790
Make sure ya let the females go so
they can lay plenty more for next year.

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:20.660
Okay.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.120
Make sure you make lots of babies, okay?

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.660
It's starting to rain harder.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:30.580
Yeah, we should probably call it soon.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.910
This should be plenty.

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:35.790
We have plenty for Ms. Sayaka, too.

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:38.160
So this was an air pump.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:40.370
They'll die without air.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:41.950
Even though we're going to eat them soon?

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.410
We're not eating them today.

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:44.450
Huh?

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:48.500
We need to wait a day to get all
the dirt out. We'll eat them tomorrow.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:53.080
I see... I thought we were
going to be able to eat them today.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.450
Ya can eat them today,

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:58.620
but they taste way better
once ya get the dirt outta them.

00:18:58.620 --> 00:19:00.000
Ah...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:03.700
Hey, Sayaka. Could ya give
us a ride to the club room?

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.790
Wait, why me?

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.750
We caught plenty of shrimps.

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:09.330
I'll be right there!

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:15.830
"The Next Day"

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:21.620
Hina and...

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:23.370
...M-Makoto's...

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:24.000
Let's Cook!

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.620
"Hina and Makoto's"
"Let's Cook!"
Let's Cook!

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:27.160
"Hina and Makoto's"
"Let's Cook!"
Let's Cook...

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:31.160
Yay!

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:34.700
Ohno-<i>senpai</i>, what are we making today?

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:38.540
Today, we're going to be deep frying
some freshwater prawn without any batter.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:47.540
First, we're going to prep the freshwater
shrimps that have been resting for a day

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:49.620
by running them under water.

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:52.540
They get jumpy, so be careful.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:57.620
Gently rinse them with water
and place the clean ones over here.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:20:00.000
Then we'll move the shrimps into
a bowl and add plenty of cooking saké.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:03.000
"Cooking Saké"
Then we'll move the shrimps into
a bowl and add plenty of cooking saké.

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:04.910
Then we'll move the shrimps into
a bowl and add plenty of cooking saké.

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:16.910
Next, you'll quickly put the lid on the bowl
so that the shrimps don't jump out.

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:18.410
Once the shrimps have calmed down,

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:24.370
you'll put them in a bag and add some
starch and make sure they get coated.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:32.290
And once you fry them up in oil at 170 degrees,

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:34.750
you're all done.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.580
Wow, they look so good!

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:40.330
Please add some salt or lemon if you'd like.

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:44.120
Let's eat!

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:55.160
What is this?! Both the flavor
and aroma are so refined!

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:57.660
Right? Aren't they great?

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:00.500
It's delicious.

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:02.660
One of the joys of the rainy season.

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:04.450
I want some beer...

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:05.580
Nope.

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.540
You meanie.

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:13.250
Maybe we should just buy yearly permits.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.250
We'll run out of club funds.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.200
We'll use Sayaka's pocket money.

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:18.500
What?

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:23.000
How much would that be for all of you? No way.

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:28.040
We promise we'll catch yer share each time, too.

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:29.790
But...

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.450
She's luring her in with shrimp...

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:33.950
Hook, line, and sinker.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:39.660
Well... If you'll let me have some beer.

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:46.450
Okay, hurry up and eat so we can leave.

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:48.250
Okay.

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.750
Make sure ya get us home, Sayaka.

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:54.410
Hey, are you even listening to me?!

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:58.120
Today's haiku...

00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:59.580
"Go river fishing.

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:01.000
But always make sure you have

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.750
your fishing permit."

00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:04.410
By Yuki.
